                        "entry_id": "570066d4-a17d-30ef-8a72-f421ead0a559",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of sour cherry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0cb51594-6637-4974-9d46-7012ae14207a",
                                "sense_id": "7fa4e0c8-a971-3f37-a141-003ec1066b66",
                                "text": "Trenner Joseph sen. & jun., Turners and Makers of agriot pipe-sticks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5f08f92-44fb-451f-9f54-b2cdb518d6e3",
                                "sense_id": "7fa4e0c8-a971-3f37-a141-003ec1066b66",
                                "text": "Comparing those plants grown in large and in samll vessels, the agriot yielded a larger amount of leaf and dry substance when grown in small vessels, whereas with the sweet cherry the reverse was the case. When grown in dilute solutions the agriot caused the evaporation through its leaves of twice as much water, and the sweet cherry under the same conditions of a third more water, than when the solutions were more concentrated."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0de13fa2-ce37-4b5b-b6c9-a4f4e1c9de4a",
                                "sense_id": "7fa4e0c8-a971-3f37-a141-003ec1066b66",
                                "text": "We distinguish between sweet cherries and sour cherries (agriots)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb0ff776-824d-4193-afc2-d663843cdf9a",
                                "sense_id": "7fa4e0c8-a971-3f37-a141-003ec1066b66",
                                "text": "On the other hand special note should be made of the cherries of Manisa, the agriots of Parsa and Gediz, and the cucumbers of Menemen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b990c44f-4604-474f-8af5-7c2eae55f523",
                                "sense_id": "7fa4e0c8-a971-3f37-a141-003ec1066b66",
                                "text": "Brandy distilled from fresh whole agriots or cherries, fermented with or without the stones."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
